.TH QJAR 1 "2026 May 14" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
qjar \- generate Java class files and a JAR from Qore modules or reflection trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qjar
[\fIoptions\fP]
[\fB\-i=\fP\fIinput_root_dir\fP | \fB\-m=\fP\fImodule\fP]
\fB\-o=\fP\fIoutput_jar\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBqjar\fR uses the Qore \fBjni\fR module to emit JVM class files corresponding
to a Qore module's public API, then packages them into a JAR.
It is part of the Qore documentation build pipeline and is also useful when
embedding Qore code in a Java host environment.
.PP
If \fB\-c\fP / \fB\-\-classes\fP is given, \fBqjar\fR walks an existing directory
tree to find pre-generated class files instead of regenerating them.
.PP
If the \fBjni\fR module is not available a warning is printed and no class
files are produced; the build continues.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-classes
Scan input for existing Java class files to include.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Do not create any output; only print paths that would be written.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input =\fIdir\fP
Root input directory (required unless \fB\-m\fP is used).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-module =\fImodule\fP
Qore module to generate class files for.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIjar\fP
Path of the JAR file to create.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help text.
